                <pb facs="0898" n="770" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg770"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 579.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to
                        Mr. Valera</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-02-27"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 27,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to quite recent correspondence,
                    touching a report of the establishment at Key West of a lottery in the interest
                    of political adventurers having designs against the peace of Cuba, I have the
                    honor to say that according to a letter of the Postmaster-General, founded on
                    official reports of his Department, there is discovered no foundation for the
                    rumor in question.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
